Description: End raw text at the appropriate end tag, in one handler
 Script, style and the raw-content elements (textarea, title and the
 rawContentTags option) are read by one handler. As in the HTML tokenizer's
 raw text states, it buffers while the text read is a case-insensitive
 prefix of "</" plus the element name, and ends the text at that prefix
 followed by whitespace, "/" or ">". Upstream matched an unanchored regular
 expression over a growing buffer, so "</" in a script string was taken into
 the close token, "</b " in a textarea left the textarea open, and
 "</script x>" did not end a script. A regular expression is no longer built
 for each character.
Author: Numiko
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Test: test/parser/parse-for-eslint.test.ts ("markup read as a browser reads it"); npm run test:upstream
Last-Update: 2026-11-04
